+# Cover letter draft — author review required
+
+**Status:** Draft, not sent. The submission category, prior-publication declaration, corresponding author, all-author consent, conflicts and affiliations require author confirmation. Do not upload this status note as a finalized declaration.
+
+Dear Editors,
+
+Please consider “FedFence: Specification-Guided Review of CI/CD Trust Changes — Two-Sided Conformance, Observation Boundaries, and Snapshot-Relative Replay” for publication as a research article in ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology.
+
+The manuscript studies the review of evolving CI/CD trust configurations against an explicit release contract. A policy change can reduce unintended admissions while excluding a required release identity; changing issuer or repository-governance assumptions can also invalidate a previously supported judgment. FedFence treats these as specification-conformance and regression-review obligations rather than classifying policy text alone.
+
+The contribution is a two-sided review method with explicit pass, fail and unknown outcomes, a state/observation account of policy-only realizability, and full-review receipts that bind and recompute the supplied contract and snapshots. The implementation retains the original FedFence regular-language representation and wrapper, with an in-place correction to character-support construction and certificate coverage checks. It does not claim a new general IAM solver, a cryptographically authenticated evidence-capture service, or end-to-end deployment verification.
+
+The evaluation combines mathematical arguments with executed offline checks: 194 regression tests, bounded projection and two-sided enumerations, 56 literal and 192 finitely bounded wildcard configurations through the strict gate, 242,580 matcher comparisons, 2,304 issuer-membership checks, three complete code-point primitive-predicate sweeps (3,342,336 comparisons), 57,498 bounded concrete/quotient matcher comparisons, 60 constructor-boundary checks, selected dependency and defect-sensitivity tests, and 54 recorded local recomputation measurements. A source-backed study separately preserves nine commits, ten role contracts and twenty-one reconstructed configurations. Twenty-four frozen source excerpts are treated as excerpts, not as completed source extractions or a representative deployment population. No real cloud account, live workflow, external tool benchmark or user-productivity study was used.
+
+The manuscript and accompanying package include source code, explicit input domains, raw results, generated plot data, reference scope records, and the current reproduction entry point. The evidence supports implementation consistency under the declared model; it does not substitute test counts for universal correctness or infer deployment outcomes from public narratives.
+
+The five listed authors are Haoyi Zhang, Huaijin Ran, Kisub Kim, Xunzhu Tang, and Tegawendé F. Bissyandé. A specific disclosure of substantial AI assistance is included in the manuscript. Before submission, the authors must supply accurate prior-submission/publication and overlap statements, select the corresponding author, verify affiliations and permissions, and confirm responsibility for the submitted content. Those declarations are intentionally not invented in this draft.
+
+Sincerely,
+
+The submitting author, after the confirmations recorded in `AUTHOR_CONFIRMATIONS.md`
