+The revised adapter validates nonempty string coordinates without coercion. It materializes iterable inputs once, preventing a generator consumed during one check from becoming an empty set in a later certificate. It applies the shared three-outcome precedence and compares complete replayed result objects rather than status alone. These changes make the local adapter consistent; they do not expand the strict gate's claimed provider coverage.
+
+The study driver records which entry point produced each public-case result. Fourteen configurations use the legacy regular-language study adapter, and seven use the finite explicit-issuer adapter. Neither count is reported as strict packet review. The distinction prevents a finite model with hand-supplied identities from being presented as a proof that an unsupported issuer profile is accepted by the operational interface.
