+\begin{proposition}[Composition under the supplied semantics]
+Suppose packet normalization preserves the supplied $M,\Phi,\pi,E$, its upper-bound interpretation is $H$ from Equation~\ref{eq:must}, every reported upper-bound proof or counterexample is sound for those sets, and the positive membership checks are exact. Suppose further that all required premises and replay checks have completed successfully. Then a \Pass{} implies
+\[
+\Adm_M(E)\subseteq M\cap\Phi\quad\text{and}\quad Q\subseteq G\cap E.
+\]
+A supported \Fail{} identifies either a state-level upper-bound violation or an intended, mintable required observation excluded by $E$.
+\end{proposition}
+\begin{proof}
+For \Pass{}, the upper-bound component establishes $G\cap E\subseteq H$, which implies the state condition by Proposition~\ref{prop:safety}. Each positive check establishes membership in $G$ and $E$, giving the second inclusion. For \Fail{}, an upper-bound witness lies in $G\cap E\setminus H$ and therefore has an unintended mintable preimage. Otherwise a missing positive is in $Q\cap G\cap H$ but not $E$. Invalid positives and failed prerequisites take priority and cannot establish this second case. The conclusion follows by the two branches of the review rule.
+\end{proof}
+
+These premises are not discharged merely by a schema label or digest. In particular, correctness of normalization and of the supplied issuer/governance abstraction remains a separate assumption. The bounded differential checks examine concrete portions of this connection. The proposition is a composition argument for those obligations, not a mechanized proof of the Python program or a theorem about a live cloud service.
